          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Hablar gave hablando. Now the other two families."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar Lens: -iendo, for both",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                ""
              ],
              "columns": 2,
              "rowCount": 4,
              "utterances": [
                "comer, comiendo.",
                "beber, bebiendo.",
                "vivir, viviendo.",
                "escribir, escribiendo."
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One ending for both. Not -endo for -er and something else for -ir — the same -iendo, every time."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "culture-pragmatics",
          "title": "Why it's said this way",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You have watched this happen before. In the preterite, the -er and -ir endings turned out to be identical, and the two families you had learned separately quietly became one."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Here it happens again, and more completely: there is not even a difference to notice. So the whole gerund is two endings for three verb families:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                ""
              ],
              "columns": 2,
              "rowCount": 2,
              "utterances": [
                "-ar verbs, -ando.",
                "everything else, -iendo."
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two endings, no agreement, no persons. It is the smallest thing this book has asked you to learn, and it unlocks the next chapter entirely."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
